// pfodWeb NOTE (correction, 2026-07-14): a previous audit pass excluded
// GPIO10-13/38-40 here, reasoning that this is the Sense variant's onboard
// camera data bus + I2S microphone (since vendor pins_arduino.h declares
// MOSI1/MISO1/SCK1, I2S_*, DVP_*, CAM_*, XMCLK on these GPIOs). Independent
// research this pass found that reasoning does not hold for the physical
// "XIAO ESP32-S3 Plus" product specifically:
//   - Seeed's own product page (seeedstudio.com/Seeed-Studio-XIAO-ESP32S3-
//     Plus-p-6361.html) states the Plus does NOT have a camera or
//     microphone (unlike the separate Sense product), and that its B2B
//     expansion connector is compatible with the Wio-SX1262 add-on board,
//     NOT the plug-in camera sensor board.
//   - The OFFICIAL upstream arduino-esp32 pins_arduino.h for this exact
//     variant folder (github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/blob/master/
//     variants/XIAO_ESP32S3_Plus/pins_arduino.h) declares D11-D19 as
//     ordinary user-facing Arduino digital pins covering exactly these
//     GPIOs (D11=38, D12=39, D13=40, D14=41, D15=42, D16=10, D17=13,
//     D18=12, D19=11) - i.e. Espressif's own board definition treats them
//     as general GPIO, not camera-exclusive. The DVP_*/CAM_*/I2S_* macro
//     names are carried over in software (same B2B connector pinout as the
//     Sense board) but do not correspond to a populated camera/mic on this
//     product.
// Corrected: GPIO10-13/38-40 restored to plain chip-level default
// capabilities (no camera/mic dedication on this board). pins_arduino.h
// restored to match the official upstream file (see NOTE there).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO10 (ADC_BAT/BAT_VOLT_PIN) - Seeed Studio forum
// (forum.seeedstudio.com/t/xiao-esp32s3-plus-adc-bat-on-gpio10/291965)
// confirms the ADC_BAT label has NO onboard voltage-divider circuit on
// this board ("I don't see any evidence that this pin is actually
// connected to the battery circuit or a voltage divider"; users report
// building their own external divider). Kept as a plain analog GPIO
// (chip default) with an informational pinNotes entry, per this repo's
// established d1_mini32/_VBAT precedent - not excluded, no ADC correction
// applied since no divider is confirmed present.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO21 tagged "led_low" - confirmed active-low user LED
// (Seeed's own docs for the XIAO ESP32-S3 line: "inverted - LOW means
// the LED is on"; independently re-confirmed this pass via Seeed's XIAO
// ESP32-S3 Plus product page: "The LED will only turn off when the user
// LED pin ... is set to a high level, and it will only turn on when the
// pin is set to a low level").
